00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:01.910
For much of the 19th
century.

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:04.940
Spike Island is one of
the most infamous prisons

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:07.580
on earth. It is
synonymous with death and

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:10.640
suffering. Gripped by
the new evidence,

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:13.220
archaeologist Kirk
French is traveling to

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:15.530
the star shaped prison
on the Irish Coast,

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:16.730
hunting for Bastion
three.

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:21.920
Much of Spike Island now
lies in ruins.

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:26.090
But at its peak, this
prison was ten times the

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:27.560
size of Alcatraz.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.280
The huge banks
surrounding the jail were

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.850
built by the inmates
themselves over 150 years

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:41.300
ago. But it's a hidden
cell block that drew

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:43.850
French here. And to find
it, he's meeting

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:46.940
archaeologist Barra
O'Donovan, an expert on

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:50.270
Spike Island. O'donovan
leads French to the

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:53.090
entrance of a series of
underground tunnels.

00:00:56.750 --> 00:00:56.900
